    "name": "Server Rules Service",
    "description": "Server Rules Service, tested through the Gateway (http://localhost:8090). The service's own REST port is not published, so the Gateway is the only way in.\n\nAUTH: nothing to set up. A collection pre-request script registers a test player (server-rules-tester@example.com) through the Gateway, logs in, and stores the JWT in the `token` variable. Every request inherits `Bearer {{token}}`. The token is refreshed automatically when it expires. If login fails, check Postman Console (View > Show Postman Console) and make sure Player Service and the Gateway are up (`docker compose ps`, `curl localhost:8090/health`).\n\nRUN ORDER: run the collection top to bottom.\n1-2. No token / invalid token -> 401 from the Gateway (proves auth is enforced at the Gateway).\n3. Get Rules -> 200.\n4. Replace Rules -> 200. NOTE: this wipes the previous rule set and replaces it with one rule.\n5-7. Validation errors: missing condition (422), missing rules field (422), malformed JSON (400).\n\nNOT COVERED HERE: the gRPC EvaluateApplicant method (host port 9091). Test it with grpcurl or a Postman gRPC request using services/server-rules-service/src/main/proto/server_rules.proto.",
